NAME
     rm - remove files and directories

SYNOPSIS
     rm [-f] [-r] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
     rm unlinks each FILE. A directory needs -r, which removes what is
     inside it first.

OPTIONS
     -f   say nothing about a name that is not there, and do not fail
     -r   remove directories and their contents

SEE ALSO
     rmdir(1), unlink(2)
